Subject: STEGA: easy veiled messages

  A couple of months ago I wrote what is an extremely inefficient and naive
approach to hiding data in ascii text. The concept is simple:
Everytime there is a break between two words (a run of spaces), 
grab the next bit from the data you want to hide and output either
one space if the bit is zero, or two spaces if the bit is one (in between
the words). The output looks like it was run through a buggy nroff, but
appears almost natural.

  
  I will now hide my name in the above paragraph using my program.

----
