Subject: a woman ahead of her time

On Fri, 23 Apr 1993, D Anton Sherwood wrote:

> Romana saith:
> > Eve ate the apple because she wanted to be as wise as god.
> 
> Hm. Is there any culture without a Promethean myth?

Probably depends on what criteria define a myth as Promethean for
you.  For example, a lot of American Indian mythologies have stories
about a culture hero stealing fire from the sky people, which is the
narrative motif of the Prometheus story.  But in the versions I know
(mostly from the Northwest) there's no suggestion that the sky
people are gods, or creators, or superior to humans, or anything
like that; they're just a bunch of selfish bastards who happen to
have something useful that they're not willing to share--so these
myths lack the "they will become like gods" theme.  (The "selfish
bastards" sounds like a Crowleyan interpretation of the Eve story, 
but doesn't have much to do with the standard version).


